1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:05,600
Follow the Rupee · Mumbai monsoon roads: Mumbai's 24 wards spend crores on monsoon road repairs. With the money left, what should be fixed first?

2
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:11,304
Built-in guide: A built-in guide rides the site like a Western line local, one stop per section.

3
00:00:11,504 --> 00:00:16,605
Stop 1 · Churchgate · The ward map: All 24 wards on one map. Darker blue means riskier open issues. Filled dots are paid for; rings are not.

4
00:00:16,805 --> 00:00:23,085
Colour and 3D: Recolour by risk, budget gap or open issues. In 3D, each ward stands as tall as its value.

5
00:00:23,285 --> 00:00:26,886
Search: Search any ward, area or road, like Sion.

6
00:00:27,086 --> 00:00:33,287
Stop 2 · Marine Lines · Ward summary: Pick a ward and the map flies there. Its summary shows open issues, cost, budget left and what to fix first.

7
00:00:33,487 --> 00:00:39,285
Stop 3 · Charni Road · The main tool: The main tool: the Next Rupee Planner. Every open issue in the ward, ranked by risk and matched to the money left.

8
00:00:39,485 --> 00:00:44,788
Budget: Start from the budget left, ₹10.9 lakh, or type any amount. At ₹5 lakh the plan recalculates instantly.

9
00:00:44,988 --> 00:00:50,791
Budget line: Each block is one repair, as wide as it costs. Dark blocks are paid for; the marker shows where money runs out.

10
00:00:50,991 --> 00:00:56,595
Two ways to spend: Riskiest first pays in rank order. Most risk covered finds the exact mix that covers the most risk.

11
00:00:56,795 --> 00:01:02,796
Show the working: Each issue gets a risk score out of 100 and a confidence level. Open one to see the arithmetic behind it.

12
00:01:02,996 --> 00:01:07,596
Your weights, tested: Change how risk is weighed and see how each weighting did against later repairs.

13
00:01:07,796 --> 00:01:12,600
The evidence behind the plan: Below the plan, the evidence: where money already went, who did the work, whether it held.

14
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:18,201
Stop 4 · Grant Road · Contractor scorecards: Contractor scorecards grade each firm against what is expected for the same work, wards and weather.

15
00:01:18,401 --> 00:01:23,602
Stop 5 · Mumbai Central · Audit: The audit flags repair bills worth a second look, not proven losses. Every flag lists its jobs.

16
00:01:23,802 --> 00:01:29,000
Stop 6 · Dadar · Complaint trail: Follow any complaint to its repair: who did it, what it cost, and whether it held.

17
00:01:29,004 --> 00:01:33,999
The planner decides where the next rupee goes. The evidence shows why. All data is synthetic; confirm on site before sending a crew.
